WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.068
Watch this dot.

2
00:00:01.348 --> 00:00:02.091
- Which one?

3
00:00:02.371 --> 00:00:05.018
Five algorithms. Five different answers.

4
00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:10.314
Same points every time. All that changes is how much you tell it.

5
00:00:10.594 --> 00:00:13.659
Start with nothing. No labels, no answer key.

6
00:00:13.939 --> 00:00:17.515
Nobody told this one the answer. Watch it guess.

7
00:00:17.795 --> 00:00:22.346
Three points drop in at random. Every dot joins the closest.

8
00:00:22.626 --> 00:00:23.183
- That's it?

9
00:00:23.463 --> 00:00:26.482
Then each slides to the middle of what it caught.

10
00:00:26.762 --> 00:00:31.824
Do that six times and the clusters stop moving. That is K-means.

11
00:00:32.104 --> 00:00:35.633
Our dot landed in cluster A. Remember that.

12
00:00:35.913 --> 00:00:39.117
Now tell it the answers. Actual numbers.

13
00:00:39.397 --> 00:00:43.623
Turn the cloud flat and you get the graph everyone knows.

14
00:00:43.903 --> 00:00:48.919
Linear regression draws one line, then measures how wrong it is.

15
00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:54.772
It tilts until those errors are as small as they go. That is best fit.

16
00:00:55.052 --> 00:00:56.306
- Ours is right on it.

17
00:00:56.586 --> 00:00:59.140
Change the question. Not how much. Which one.

18
00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.668
The line lifts off the floor into a curve. Height is probability.

19
00:01:04.947 --> 00:01:05.876
- Same thing?

20
00:01:06.156 --> 00:01:09.082
No. That gave a number. This gives a chance.

21
00:01:09.362 --> 00:01:13.867
Our dot came out at fifty percent. It refused to answer.

22
00:01:14.147 --> 00:01:16.887
Four of these five lose to the fifth.

23
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.653
- Then why learn the four?

24
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:22.927
Because the fifth one is all four of them, stacked.

25
00:01:23.207 --> 00:01:27.619
A tree stops drawing lines. It cuts the space into boxes.

26
00:01:27.898 --> 00:01:31.474
Bigger than that? Go left. Late at night? Go right.

27
00:01:31.754 --> 00:01:37.745
Every leaf is a box. Ours fell in box three. Box three says A.

28
00:01:38.025 --> 00:01:40.811
Which is why a tree can show its working.

29
00:01:41.091 --> 00:01:46.432
One tree is a weak guess. So build another that fixes its mistakes.

30
00:01:46.712 --> 00:01:48.988
Then another. Then three hundred.

31
00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.428
- Three hundred?

32
00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:56.513
Each one small, each correcting the last. The boundary gets jagged, and right.

33
00:01:56.793 --> 00:02:03.016
That is boosted trees. On this cloud it beat the flat plane by five points.

34
00:02:03.296 --> 00:02:06.361
Our dot? Three hundred votes. Class B.

35
00:02:06.641 --> 00:02:13.932
Same dot, five times. Cluster A. On the line. A coin flip. Box three. Class B.

36
00:02:14.213 --> 00:02:15.513
- So which one was right?

37
00:02:15.793 --> 00:02:22.016
The last one. The truth was B. We picked a hard point; the easy ones agree.

38
00:02:22.296 --> 00:02:26.801
One cloud. Five shapes. All that changed is how much you told it.

39
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.145
Comment ALGO for all five on one page.
